definitions.construction:
Arbitrarily fix once and for all one deterministic witness bank whose existence is supplied by \(\text{lem:finite-contour-bank}\).  Conditional on that fixed bank, form \(\widehat F_{a,n}\) and \(\widehat G_{a,n}\) on \(I_a\).  Declare \(j\) pilot-admissible when \(\inf_{z\in C_j}|\widehat F_{0,n}(z)|\ge a_{\star}/2\) and \(\widehat N_{0j,n}\ge1\).  Let \(\widehat j_n\) be the smallest index among the admissible maximizers of \(\inf_{z\in C_j}|\widehat F_{0,n}(z)|\).  Return zero if there is no admissible index or if \(\inf_{z\in C_{\widehat j_n}}|\widehat F_{1,n}(z)|<a_{\star}/4\); otherwise set
\[
 \widehat\theta_{\mathrm{spec},n}
 =\Pi_{[-C_{\theta},C_{\theta}]}
 \operatorname{Re}\!\left[
 \frac{1}{\widehat N_{0\widehat j_n,n}2\pi i}
 \oint_{C_{\widehat j_n}}
 \frac{\widehat G_{1,n}(z)}{\widehat F_{1,n}(z)}\,dz
 \right].
\]
All circles use fixed parameterizations, and all ties and failures use the displayed deterministic rules.  After the arbitrary witness bank has been fixed, this is a measurable sample map.  The observations and displayed class constants do not furnish an algorithm for obtaining the bank, its radii, or \(a_{\star}\); no effective construction, enumeration, or learning of them is asserted.

statements.statement:
For \(s\ge r+1\),
\[
 \mathcal P_{\mathrm{NG},n}^{\mathrm{ACE}}
 \subseteq\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}},
\]
because both \(L^s(P_X)\) supplied-code restrictions imply their \(L^r(P_X)\) counterparts. Neither \(\mathcal P_{\mathrm{NG},n}\subseteq\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) nor equality of the broad spectral and published ACE classes is asserted. If \(\mathsf E_n^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) holds and \(\varepsilon_{1,n}>0\), then, for every \(\varepsilon_{2,n}\ge0\), with \(\varepsilon_{2,n}=0\) obtained by monotone boundary extension,
\[
\begin{aligned}
 &\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm{NG},n}^{\mathrm{ACE}}}
 Q_{P,1-\gamma}(|\widehat\theta_{\mathrm{ACE},r,n}-\theta_0(P)|)\\
 &\quad\le B_{\mathrm{ACE},n,\gamma}\\
 &\quad=C_{\gamma}r!16^r\delta^{-1}
 \Big[\varepsilon_{1,n}^r\varepsilon_{2,n}
 +C_{\theta}\varepsilon_{1,n}^{r+1}
 +64(C_g+\psi_{\eta})^r
 \{r^2(C_g+\psi_{\eta})+\psi_{\xi}+C_{\theta}\psi_{\eta}\}
 (\gamma n)^{-1/2}\Big].
\end{aligned}
\]
If also \(n\ge2\) and \(\varepsilon_{1,n}\le\varepsilon_0\), the spectral generalized-quantile guarantee holds on \(\mathcal P_{\mathrm{NG},n}^{\mathrm{ACE}}\); whenever \(\varepsilon_{1,n}^r\varepsilon_{2,n}+C_{\theta}\varepsilon_{1,n}^{r+1}\gg n^{-1/2}\), that spectral upper guarantee is strictly smaller in order than \(B_{\mathrm{ACE},n,\gamma}\). This is a comparison of upper guarantees, not a lower bound for ACE.

If \(\mathsf E_n^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) holds and \(\varepsilon_{1,n},\varepsilon_{2,n}>0\), Jin--Mackey--Syrgkanis Theorem 5.4 gives, on \(\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\),
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 &\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}}
 Q_{P,1-\gamma}(|\widehat\theta_{\mathrm{ACE},r,n}-\theta_0(P)|)\\
 &\quad\le C_{\gamma}r!16^r\delta^{-1}
 \Big[\varepsilon_{1,n}^r\varepsilon_{2,n}
 +C_{\theta}\varepsilon_{1,n}^{r+1}
 +64(C_g+\psi_{\eta})^r
 \{r^2(C_g+\psi_{\eta})+\psi_{\xi}+C_{\theta}\psi_{\eta}\}
 (\gamma n)^{-1/2}\Big].
 \end{aligned}
\]

